---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"
---

<Layout
  title="FixMyImport Privacy | Browser-first CSV processing"
  description="How FixMyImport handles CSV files, local processing, and lightweight analytics in the first release."
>
  <main class="w-full px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p class="text-base font-medium tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">
            Privacy
          </p>
          <h1
            class="text-3xl leading-tight font-semibold tracking-wide sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl"
          >
            Local by default, narrow by design.
          </h1>
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
            FixMyImport is built as a browser-first CSV utility. The default
            experience does not upload files or store CSV contents on a server.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 text-base text-muted-foreground">
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-wide text-foreground">
              CSV handling
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              CSV parsing, cleanup, dedupe, preview generation, splitting, and
              export preparation all run locally in the browser.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-wide text-foreground">
              Analytics
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              The app is wired for privacy-friendly event hooks only. File
              contents, column names, and row data are not sent as analytics
              properties.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-border/70 bg-background/70 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-wide text-foreground">
              Commercial layer
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              The no-auth Pro flow stores a lightweight unlock token in local
              storage. Hosted checkout can be connected later without turning
              the app into an account system.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
